t83|n|In Anglo-Saxon times, the people of a group of townships or villages; a community; a tribe. ; People in general, or a separate class of people; -- generally used in the plural form, and often with a qualifying adjective; as, the old folks; poor folks. ; The persons of one's own family; as, our folks are all well.	a:2bnh,65,3;1c35,22,6;18zh,21,5;1fwy,18,8~1fwy,18,8;1c35,22,6;18zh,21,5;2bnh,65,3	v:1uqn,38,5~1uqn,38,5	V:22yl,45,3;1uqb,32,4;28ad,20,6;289v,17,7~289v,17,7;28ad,20,6;1uqb,32,4;22yl,45,3
