t8d|a|Next after; succeeding; ensuing; as, the assembly was held on the following day. ; (In the field of a telescope) In the direction from which stars are apparently moving (in consequence of the earth's rotation); as, a small star, north following or south following. In the direction toward which stars appear to move is called preceding.	j:ffp,45,2;1ekb,30,1;1z72,28,2;10gu,26,12;bf3,25,1;1n0u,22,2;130b,21,3;ex0,21,2;1k0m,20,5;1k0p,19,2;738,17,3;176t,15,11;1ppu,14,5;rg5,12,2;1zf3,11,4~10gu,26,12;176t,15,11;1vf8,6,7;1k0m,20,5;1ppu,14,5;17br,7,5;1zf3,11,4;130b,21,3;4u8,6,3;738,17,3;1wl6,3,3;eaw,10,3;1z72,28,2;1k0p,19,2;rg5,12,2
